    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "An antonym is a word that expresses a meaning directly opposite to another word.",
        "The antonym of a word must strictly belong to the same part of speech (e.g., noun for noun, verb for verb).",
        "Common prefixes such as 'un-', 'dis-', 'in-', 'im-', and 'non-' are frequently used to form antonyms.",
        "Root words, prefixes, and suffixes serve as effective tools for eliminating wrong options in vocabulary tests."
      ],
      "id": "nkoq9eo"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Examiners often place synonyms among the options to confuse candidates who read hastily.",
        "Always check for contextual meaning, as words with multiple meanings have different antonyms depending on usage.",
        "Eliminate options that belong to a different part of speech even if their general meaning seems opposite."
      ],
      "id": "l87uecl"
    },
